  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 104 AM MDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\n|Low pressure will settle over eastern Idaho today. Will \nprobably see a mix of sun and clouds today with occasional light\nrain showers and isolated thunderstorms. The heavy rains that \nwe have around the past couple days should be over. Additional \nrainfall amounts range from a couple hundredths to 0.10 inches. \nTemps will be cooler with highs ranging from the upper 50s to \nmid 60s. Skies will clear this evening which will allow \ntemperatures to fall a bit more than we had seen in previous \nmodel runs. Right now, temps look like they will hold in the \nupper 30s for the Snake Plain and Magic Valley, but the trend is\nabout 5 degrees cooler than what we saw on Thursday night's \nmodel runs. Same holds true for Sunday night. Sunday looks dry \nbut any clouds we have will quickly clear in the evening and the\nmodels have lowered the temps about 5 degrees. So potentially \nif these trends continue we could need frost advisories. Right \nnow, it looks like mainly a patchy frost problem. \n\nAs we move into midweek, a low pressure system will move into the \ncentral Great Basin. This low is expected to weaken and lift \nnorthward into our area. So we could see some isolated showers now \nfrom this system that we weren't seeing in previous model solutions. \nBut as a whole, next week looks dry with temps returning to slightly \nabove normal by end week.",
